# Read by oxfmt (it picks up .gitignore and .prettierignore by default);
# this repo does not use prettier itself.
#
# Changelogs are generated by release-please on every release. Formatting
# them is not ours to do — the generator rewrites the file wholesale on
# the next release, and a formatter that disagrees with it fails CI on
# every release PR.
CHANGELOG.md
**/CHANGELOG.md

# The example project's mocks are written by laqi itself, from the panel and
# from MCP, with `JSON.stringify(value, null, 2)`. The formatter disagrees
# with that on short arrays, so every session spent trying the panel against
# examples/todo-app turned `bun run verify` red on a file nobody typed.
examples/*/laqi/*.json
examples/*/.laqi/*.json

# Characterization goldens. They are written by the test that reads them, with
# `JSON.stringify(value, null, 2)`, and are the oracle the JSON Schema compiler
# is held to. A formatter that reflows them would make the test rewrite them
# again on the next run, and the pair would never agree.
packages/generate/goldens/
